Natural-language invocation grammar

You would not need formal commands. Ordinary language calls the tools:

“Look around”              → Cloud.Eyes + Cloud.Map
“Find a way”               → Cloud.Route
“Make it happen”           → Cloud.Quest + Cloud.Hands
“Check whether it worked”  → Cloud.Verify
“Keep watching”            → Cloud.Watch
“Give me control”          → Cloud.Handoff
“Add this to Pantheon”      → Cloud.Memory + Cloud.Return
“Prove it isn’t just luck” → Reality.Forker + Blinded Battery
“Release it into the wild” → Seed.Distiller + Mutation.Returner
“Trust the plan”            → continue the active quest within its authorized boundaries

The key invention is not another button. It is the tool-selection grammar that turns language into situated play.

The cloud supplies terrain.
The primitives supply legal moves.
The Golden Thread supplies continuity.
The Money Bin retains accumulated value.
The Blinded Battery keeps the game honest.
And the CogOS becomes the player that can cross between all of them.